Computer Science Distinguished Lecture

When the Test Set Lies: Robust Learning Under Distribution Shift
Monday, March 2, 2026 | 3:30-4:45 PM | Goodwin Hall 155
Speaker: Prof. S. Varga, Department of Statistics and Data Science

Abstract: Benchmarks report accuracy on held-out data drawn from the training=
 distribution, but deployed models meet hospitals, cities and users that diff=
er from the training set. This talk covers three practical tools: grouped and=
 temporal splits that expose leakage, importance-weighted validation, and a s=
imple stress-testing protocol that has caught overstated results in published=
 work.

Reception to follow in the Goodwin atrium.
